      "narrative": "The copper lamps hiss softly as you turn to the woman in the charcoal coat. She's been nursing the same half-empty mug since you arrived, her sharp eyes tracking the room with a patience that suggests she's done this before.\n\nYou ask about the Ash Gate.\n\nMara Venn's expression flickers \u2014 a brief tightening around the eyes \u2014 before she sets her mug down with a soft clack. She looks at you, then past you, toward the shuttered window that faces the direction of the gate.\n\n\"The Ash Gate.\" She says the words like she's testing their weight. \"What's your business with it?\"\n\nShe's deflecting. You can feel it \u2014 she knows something, but your question was too broad, too unfocused. You asked *what she knows* instead of *what she's seen*, and she's seized the gap to size you up before committing to an answer.\n\nBehind the bar, Toran Vex's ink-stained fingers freeze on the ledger he's pretending to read. He's listening. Hard.\n\nMara leans forward, elbows on the scarred table. The lamplight carves shadows across her face.\n\n\"Let's try again,\" she says, her voice low. \"What exactly are you looking for at the Ash Gate, ranger?\""
    },
