      "narrative": "The question comes out too sharp, too insistent. You lean across the table, your voice pressing \u2014 demanding a name, demanding the truth \u2014 and Mara Venn's face goes cold.\n\nShe doesn't answer.\n\nInstead, she pushes her empty mug to the center of the table with a deliberate scrape of ceramic on wood. Her sharp eyes fix on you, and something in them has shuttered \u2014 the brief openness from a moment ago, gone.\n\n\"I think we're done here.\"\n\nShe stands. The chair legs scrape the floorboards.\n\nBehind the bar, Toran Vex looks up from his ledger \u2014 not pretending anymore. His nervous eyes dart between you and Mara, and his hand drifts toward something beneath the counter. His fingers wrap around what might be a handle.\n\nMara Venn buttons her charcoal coat, not looking at you. \"You ask too many questions with too little coin behind 'em, ranger. Come back when you've got something to trade.\"\n\nShe steps past your table toward the door.\n\nToran Vex's hand stays where it is \u2014 beneath the counter, gripping something. He's watching you, not Mara. His breath comes shallow and quick.\n\nThe tavern settles into a heavy, waiting silence."
