      "narrative": "The Copper Finch's door groans open. Warm air spills out \u2014 smoke, spilled ale, the faint salt of old sweat. A few heads turn. A man in a patched coat eyes you from the bar, then looks away.\n\nYour table stands where you left it. Near the window. Scarred wood. A salt cellar crusted with use.\n\nYou sit.\n\nThe chair creaks. The tavern settles back into its low murmur \u2014 conversations that paused when you entered, now resuming. A log shifts in the hearth. Somewhere in the back, a pot clangs.\n\nMara Venn's table is empty. Her mug is gone.\n\nToran Vex stands behind the bar, polishing a glass with a rag that's seen better days. He hasn't looked up since you walked in. His hands move in tight, mechanical circles \u2014 the same motion repeated too many times, a man buying time behind busywork.\n\nThe hearth fire pops. A drop of condensation runs down the window glass.\n\nNo one approaches your table. No one meets your eye. The tavern lets you sit, but it doesn't welcome you back."
